1
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:06,000
I wonder if that man, Hiraku Machio,
has been doing well.

2
00:00:06,791 --> 00:00:10,750
Having wondered how he was faring,
I decided to observe him.

3
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:12,833
I am God.

4
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:16,000
The salvation of souls is part of my job.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,291
However, even God makes mistakes.

6
00:00:19,291 --> 00:00:26,708
I mistakenly bestowed a life of suffering
fit for a sinner upon an innocent man.

7
00:00:27,041 --> 00:00:30,791
Interfering after someone has
started their life is against the rules.

8
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:32,958
In an attempt to make up for what I'd done,

9
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:36,416
I gave him a chance at a second life
per his wishes, however...

10
00:00:38,291 --> 00:00:42,458
Isn't this forest in a dangerous area
filled with wicked nasty monsters?

11
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:44,833
I'm pretty sure it's called
The Forest of Death...

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,458
He was thrown in there all alone
and told to sustain himself by farming.

13
00:00:48,458 --> 00:00:50,125
What kind of twisted game is this?!

14
00:00:50,125 --> 00:00:52,125
I need to call him back right away... but no!

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,125
I just said that would be
an infraction of the rules!

16
00:00:55,625 --> 00:00:59,500
There's a chance he'll find his way
back here again as a soul.

17
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,500
If that happens, I hope he accepts my apology.

18
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:04,833
Even God... makes mistakes.

19
00:01:15,291 --> 00:01:17,291
Farming Life in Another World

20
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:39,458
Here are the results from me having used
the almighty farming tool for a while.

21
00:02:39,458 --> 00:02:41,458
I've been able to learn several things.

22
00:02:42,125 --> 00:02:45,833
First, there are the crops that I was able
to grow without planting any seeds.

23
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:47,250
There are potatoes,

24
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:48,708
onions,

25
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:50,291
tomatoes, and...

26
00:02:50,583 --> 00:02:52,083
cabbage as well as others.

27
00:02:52,083 --> 00:02:57,500
These are the exact plants I was thinking about
while I was tilling the land earlier.

28
00:02:57,875 --> 00:03:01,375
- Eggplant! Eggplant! Eggplant! Eggplant!
- If I imagine the plants I want to grow
while I'm using the almighty farming tool,

29
00:03:01,375 --> 00:03:03,333
those seeds become sowed in the ground.

30
00:03:03,458 --> 00:03:05,083
I... want... spinach!

31
00:03:05,083 --> 00:03:08,083
When I looked for proof so that
I could put this theory to the test...

32
00:03:08,083 --> 00:03:09,333
here's what happened.

33
00:03:10,208 --> 00:03:12,583
I wanted something that I'd be able
to identify as soon as it sprouted,

34
00:03:12,583 --> 00:03:16,875
- Bean sprouts! Bean sprouts! Bean sprouts!
- so I thought about how much
I wanted soybeans while I was tilling.

35
00:03:16,875 --> 00:03:18,041
Bean sprouts!

36
00:03:18,541 --> 00:03:21,083
And that's exactly what I got.

37
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:23,750
I'm sure these will continue
growing into soybeans.

38
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:27,791
For now, I'll just sit back and watch.

39
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:31,875
Crops I planted with the almighty
farming tool grow very quickly.

40
00:03:32,916 --> 00:03:37,125
Actually, sometimes they grow so fast I find
myself thinking "Oh crap!" after they pop up.

41
00:03:37,666 --> 00:03:40,041
These potatoes, for example, turned green
where the sun was hitting them.

42
00:03:40,041 --> 00:03:41,833
If my memory serves correctly,
potato sprouts are poisonous.

43
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:42,833
I'm too afraid to try eating these.

44
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:44,291
To prevent this from happening again,

45
00:03:44,291 --> 00:03:47,541
I think it's best to put a little mound of soil
near the plant's base.

46
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:51,416
I didn't have any idea what I was going on
when I looked at crops in my previous life,

47
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:56,000
but I'm sure the farmers had all kinds of
knowledge they learned from their experiences.

48
00:03:56,250 --> 00:03:59,250
My only option now is to press on
and learn from my mistakes.

49
00:04:00,916 --> 00:04:04,041
Anyways, the only reason I'm able to
live a life of farming here

50
00:04:04,041 --> 00:04:05,500
is by the grace of the Gods.

51
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:09,041
That's why I decided to make
some statues of them.

52
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:10,416
Just so you know,

53
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:13,000
the one on the left is supposed to be
the God with jurisdiction over agriculture.

54
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:16,166
It feels like things are getting
more civilized around here.

55
00:04:16,166 --> 00:04:17,875
Thank you, Gods.

56
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:22,625
I'm living a very primitive lifestyle here.

57
00:04:23,166 --> 00:04:25,666
Today's lunch is a stew
made from rabbit meat

58
00:04:25,666 --> 00:04:28,250
and super fresh farm-to-table vegetables
grown without any pesticides!

59
00:04:28,250 --> 00:04:30,000
In other words, I just boiled stuff.

60
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,750
I don't have anything to season it with.

61
00:04:31,958 --> 00:04:33,958
Mmmm, organic.

62
00:04:33,958 --> 00:04:36,291
Plus the meat from the animals
is a lot easier to eat

63
00:04:36,291 --> 00:04:38,291
if I drain the blood as soon as I kill them.

64
00:04:39,208 --> 00:04:42,125
The dogs like eating the meat from the animals
I drained the blood from properly, too.

65
00:04:42,458 --> 00:04:45,208
Sometimes I worry that
I've spoiled them with this food.

66
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:48,916
Oh well. As long as they're enjoying it,
then it's fine.

67
00:04:50,125 --> 00:04:52,500
I wish I had some salt, though.

68
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:55,250
I decided to try my hand at something new.

69
00:04:55,916 --> 00:04:58,958
I know it's hard to tell now,
but I planted some fruit bearing trees here.

70
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:02,791
- If this goes well,
my diet will instantly improve, but...
- Apples!

71
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:03,666
Pears! Pears!

72
00:05:03,666 --> 00:05:06,375
...they say that fruit trees take years
to bear fruit, so I'll need patience.

73
00:05:06,375 --> 00:05:07,541
Persimmons!

74
00:05:08,125 --> 00:05:09,625
I'm prepared to wait as long as I need to.

75
00:05:09,625 --> 00:05:10,458
Go!

76
00:05:13,291 --> 00:05:15,208
Good boy! Good boy!

77
00:05:16,041 --> 00:05:18,458
Life with the dogs is really fun.

78
00:05:18,958 --> 00:05:23,208
The loneliness might have been unbearable
if I didn't have them here.

79
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:25,375
A horn?

80
00:05:25,375 --> 00:05:29,083
Well, I am in a different world.
I guess dogs have horns here.

81
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:33,875
They're all waiting their turn.

82
00:05:35,083 --> 00:05:38,125
There's another thing that having the dogs
here really helps out with.

83
00:05:39,541 --> 00:05:42,916
They can travel through the forest
without getting lost.

84
00:05:43,458 --> 00:05:46,291
Thanks to that, I can explore
even further into the forest.

85
00:05:46,916 --> 00:05:48,000
And eventually...

86
00:05:49,583 --> 00:05:52,083
I found a river that could
act as a source of water.

87
00:05:52,083 --> 00:05:55,000
There's a little waterfall upstream
that raises the river up a level.

88
00:05:55,541 --> 00:05:58,750
I think I might be able to dig out a path
for that water to run to my home.

89
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:02,166
It's a 30-minute walk,
so I'd have to do a lot of digging...

90
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:04,541
but it'll be fine
if I work at it little by little.

91
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,166
I figured I'd be working away
from home for a while,

92
00:06:07,166 --> 00:06:09,041
so I built myself a toilet
at the construction site.

93
00:06:09,041 --> 00:06:11,083
Yup. Nice and civilized.

94
00:06:17,291 --> 00:06:19,875
I turned the almighty farming tool
into a wheelbarrow.

95
00:06:19,875 --> 00:06:22,750
I don't tire out at all while using
the almighty farming tool,

96
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:27,083
so now I can travel around without
getting tired and speed up construction.

97
00:06:32,125 --> 00:06:34,625
I think I need to fix the roads first.

98
00:06:38,416 --> 00:06:39,666
Back at the home base,

99
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:43,291
I've cleared out more of the forest
and continued expanding my crop fields.

100
00:06:43,875 --> 00:06:45,916
I'm growing oilseed rape crops
to harvest their oil.

101
00:06:45,916 --> 00:06:47,291
It's the plant rapeseed oil comes from.

102
00:06:47,666 --> 00:06:48,666
Wheat.

103
00:06:48,666 --> 00:06:49,875
It's easy to preserve,

104
00:06:49,875 --> 00:06:52,250
and I can use it for all kinds of
different stuff if I turn it into flour.

105
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:55,416
Sugarcane, because I want something sweet...

106
00:06:55,875 --> 00:06:59,166
By the way, those bean sprouts
grew into soybeans before I knew it.

107
00:06:59,166 --> 00:07:01,333
I wanted to eat some edamame, but...

108
00:07:02,291 --> 00:07:05,125
I need salt to make it,
and I don't have any.

109
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:08,291
I wonder if there's any rock salt around here.

110
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,083
Farming Life in Another World.

111
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:12,416
FRUIT TREES
RIVER AND WATERFALL
NEW CROP FIELDS

112
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:17,250
How long has it been
since I started living here?

113
00:07:22,041 --> 00:07:24,208
One day, it started to get cold.

114
00:07:24,666 --> 00:07:27,208
Honestly, it's too cold
to be in these clothes now.

115
00:07:27,875 --> 00:07:30,125
I can see snow on the mountains
in the distance.

116
00:07:30,125 --> 00:07:32,958
I wonder how cold the winters here get.

117
00:07:33,833 --> 00:07:36,416
I need to do something
to prepare for the cold.

118
00:07:37,458 --> 00:07:40,500
I tried to use the pelt from the giant rabbits,

119
00:07:40,916 --> 00:07:42,750
but they smelled awful

120
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:45,458
and I was worried that they would
start rotting, so I gave up on them.

121
00:07:45,958 --> 00:07:49,000
I guess my only option is to
light a fire a stay inside my hut.

122
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,458
I'll need to gather firewood
and food for the winter.

123
00:07:57,875 --> 00:08:00,250
A giant black seat cushion?

124
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,333
Wait, is that a spider?

125
00:08:11,791 --> 00:08:14,041
This looks like some really nice cloth.

126
00:08:14,041 --> 00:08:15,291
Is it a handkerchief?

127
00:08:15,291 --> 00:08:17,083
They even embroidered it!

128
00:08:17,375 --> 00:08:19,500
That's amazing. Thank you.

129
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:24,083
The spider started living up in the giant tree.

130
00:08:24,583 --> 00:08:26,666
And their favorite food is potatoes.

131
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:30,666
It's not just cloth,
they can even make clothes really well.

132
00:08:31,125 --> 00:08:34,791
They actually managed to turn the animal pelts
I'd given up on into some nice stuff.

133
00:08:35,791 --> 00:08:37,708
I can handle the cold with this!

134
00:08:39,416 --> 00:08:40,916
Bedding stuffed with leaves!

135
00:08:40,916 --> 00:08:41,750
CIVILIZATION

136
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,291
Curtains that block the wind!

137
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:44,291
CIVILIZATION

138
00:08:44,708 --> 00:08:48,833
Just having stuff made from cloth now
has made this place much more civilized.

139
00:08:49,583 --> 00:08:51,416
By the way, I gave the spider a name.

140
00:08:51,416 --> 00:08:53,500
Based on my first impression,
I called them Zabuton.

141
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,333
ZABUTON
(CUSHION)

142
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:56,333
Now I have someone else
I can count on living here.

143
00:08:59,125 --> 00:09:01,208
Winter finally arrived.

144
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,750
It's gotten pretty cold outside,

145
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:06,833
but thanks to the preparations I made,
I'll make it through fine.

146
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:09,583
The dogs are all cozy inside.

147
00:09:09,916 --> 00:09:12,041
Zabuton might be hibernating or something,

148
00:09:12,041 --> 00:09:13,875
because they haven't come down
from the tree lately.

149
00:09:16,041 --> 00:09:19,875
It snows here, but thankfully
it doesn't pile up too much.

150
00:09:19,875 --> 00:09:23,500
If this region got heavy snow fall,
it would have already flattened my hut.

151
00:09:27,041 --> 00:09:29,083
I am still a little worried.

152
00:09:29,708 --> 00:09:32,416
The food stored ahead of time
should be enough to last.

153
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:37,166
I don't have any real problems living here now,
but I do wish I had some salt.

154
00:09:37,916 --> 00:09:42,250
For some reason I've been feeling
really lonely lately.

155
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,916
It's cold...

156
00:09:46,666 --> 00:09:50,541
How long has it been
since I've talked to someone?

157
00:09:51,291 --> 00:09:54,000
At this rate, I might forget how to talk.

158
00:09:56,583 --> 00:09:58,750
Eventually, the cold started to ease up.

159
00:09:59,041 --> 00:10:00,833
The snow began to melt.

160
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:03,166
And before long, it felt like spring.

161
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:10,583
Around that time, something was
happening with the puppies.

162
00:10:10,833 --> 00:10:12,875
They all entered the forest.

163
00:10:12,875 --> 00:10:15,083
It was time for them to leave the nest.

164
00:10:15,083 --> 00:10:18,958
Seeing them grow up so well
brought me some joy, and some sadness.

165
00:10:20,958 --> 00:10:23,000
As I found myself starting to get lost
in those kinds of thoughts...

166
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,333
This is nature...

167
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:28,083
They came back a few days later.

168
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:30,916
Apparently, they had all gone
looking for partners.

169
00:10:31,708 --> 00:10:34,375
I wonder if he got into a fight with a rival.

170
00:10:34,875 --> 00:10:36,875
It's not easy being a dog.

171
00:10:37,625 --> 00:10:39,583
And there was one more surprise.

172
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:45,583
After not having seen them for a while,
Zabuton showed up with a bunch of kids.

173
00:10:46,625 --> 00:10:48,416
I guess she was a female...

174
00:10:48,708 --> 00:10:51,125
Well, this is all good news.

175
00:10:51,916 --> 00:10:55,666
Everyone has a bigger family now.
To be honest, I'm jealous.

176
00:10:58,791 --> 00:11:00,833
And so, there were more mouths to feed.

177
00:11:00,833 --> 00:11:03,916
That meant it was time to work even harder
at expanding my crop fields.

178
00:11:08,291 --> 00:11:09,416
That's...

179
00:11:12,041 --> 00:11:13,916
Zabuton's ringing the alarm?

180
00:11:13,916 --> 00:11:16,000
Is something nasty heading this way?

181
00:11:22,916 --> 00:11:26,041
Kuro led me into the middle of the forest.

182
00:11:26,791 --> 00:11:29,916
Meeting someone new
always happens as a surprise.

183
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:35,583
That's definitely...

184
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:37,708
a little girl.

185
00:11:37,708 --> 00:11:39,833
Why is she in the middle of the forest here?

186
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,375
Why is she in this condition?

187
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:49,583
Hey, wait!

188
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:51,500
Help me! Please!

189
00:11:51,666 --> 00:11:53,375
We can understand each other...

190
00:11:53,375 --> 00:11:54,375
Okay.

191
00:11:54,708 --> 00:11:57,125
I'm not sure what's going on here,

192
00:11:58,416 --> 00:12:01,916
but it's been a long time since I've heard
someone else's voice.

193
00:12:24,666 --> 00:12:26,208
She grew?

194
00:12:27,708 --> 00:12:29,583
Thank you for saving me.

195
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,625
Who the heck is she?

196
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:34,833
Is she a monster or
something dangerous like that?

197
00:12:41,583 --> 00:12:43,791
Wait! No! Stop!

198
00:12:43,791 --> 00:12:46,375
Stop it! Paw! Wait, I mean sit!

199
00:12:49,166 --> 00:12:51,166
She got small again.

200
00:12:51,541 --> 00:12:56,750
So... like, are you... my enemy?

201
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,541
Are you here to hurt us?

202
00:12:58,541 --> 00:13:01,791
No! Stop siccing your dogs on me!

203
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:03,791
But you sucked my blood just now.

204
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:06,708
I'm sorry, but I couldn't help it!

205
00:13:06,708 --> 00:13:08,250
It's because of them!

206
00:13:09,125 --> 00:13:11,041
Come on, stop it!

207
00:13:14,625 --> 00:13:16,708
Well, she seems harmless enough.

208
00:13:17,375 --> 00:13:21,166
According to her, us meeting
was a complete coincidence.

209
00:13:21,583 --> 00:13:24,750
And the reason she sucked my blood
was to recover her strength.

210
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,583
She said that she used too much energy

211
00:13:26,583 --> 00:13:29,416
and couldn't maintain her body form
or her clothes anymore.

212
00:13:29,958 --> 00:13:33,625
Why did they all even attack her
in the first place?

213
00:13:34,291 --> 00:13:37,541
I thought I could take on one of them...

214
00:13:37,541 --> 00:13:40,875
Okay then. So she was the one
who attacked first.

215
00:13:41,125 --> 00:13:44,875
That said, I felt bad at how hard
they'd beaten her up,

216
00:13:44,875 --> 00:13:48,500
so I offered to let her suck some more
of my blood so that she could recover.

217
00:13:51,416 --> 00:13:54,583
It feels like she's
sucking a lot of my blood...

218
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,833
but I don't feel any effects from it at all.

219
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:59,833
Is this another one of the perks
of a healthy body?

220
00:14:05,958 --> 00:14:08,833
I've never tasted blood so full of vitality!

221
00:14:08,833 --> 00:14:11,250
You must be living a healthy life.

222
00:14:12,333 --> 00:14:13,333
What?

223
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,583
Aren't you smaller than last time?

224
00:14:16,583 --> 00:14:19,875
Huh? But if I suck any more of your blood,
your life will be in danger.

225
00:14:19,875 --> 00:14:22,333
Don't worry about it.
Take as much as you want.

226
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:23,541
O-okay...

227
00:14:28,458 --> 00:14:31,875
I can't believe there's a place like this
in the middle of this forest!

228
00:14:32,166 --> 00:14:34,708
Are all of these crops yours?

229
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:38,666
I've never seen this plant before.

230
00:14:39,875 --> 00:14:41,375
What's this?

231
00:14:41,375 --> 00:14:43,083
The one here with the red fruit.

232
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:44,875
They're very pretty.

233
00:14:44,875 --> 00:14:46,500
Are they decorative plants?

234
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:49,041
They're tomatoes.
Have you never seen them?

235
00:14:49,041 --> 00:14:50,750
No, this is the first time.

236
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:53,791
I see. I guess they aren't normal here.

237
00:14:57,458 --> 00:14:59,833
Let's see. Which one looks good?

238
00:15:01,083 --> 00:15:03,000
Here. Want to try one?

239
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,500
You can eat them just like that?

240
00:15:12,083 --> 00:15:14,541
The texture is strange, but...

241
00:15:15,875 --> 00:15:17,333
it tastes wonderful!

242
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,791
It's so juicy!

243
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:22,666
It really is nice to hear
someone praise your work.

244
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:27,041
Hey, I want to see your other crops.

245
00:15:27,166 --> 00:15:28,166
Sure.

246
00:15:58,291 --> 00:16:00,583
I never imagined that I'd ever
be able to learn about

247
00:16:00,583 --> 00:16:03,166
so many new species in a single day!

248
00:16:04,041 --> 00:16:06,583
I guess that thing is magic.

249
00:16:06,583 --> 00:16:08,208
Makes sense. I'm in a different world.

250
00:16:08,875 --> 00:16:11,375
Her name is Lu Lulucy.

251
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:13,250
She's a vampire.

252
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:17,125
Well, she already sucked a lot of my blood
so I shouldn't really be surprised now.

253
00:16:17,416 --> 00:16:21,125
She said that she's doing
research on medicinal plants.

254
00:16:21,125 --> 00:16:23,250
And the reason she came to this forest was...

255
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,500
I got into a little fight with some nobles.

256
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:28,625
They were trying to steal
my research away from me.

257
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:32,916
After I ran away, they sent a real
pain in the ass to chase me down.

258
00:16:32,916 --> 00:16:37,208
I decided it would be best for me to
lay low somewhere until things cooled off.

259
00:16:37,791 --> 00:16:40,291
That's when I heard about this forest.

260
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,708
I thought coming here might
help along my research as well,

261
00:16:42,708 --> 00:16:44,250
but this is more than I imagined.

262
00:16:44,458 --> 00:16:47,916
I wonder how many days it'll take me
to inspect everything here.

263
00:16:47,916 --> 00:16:49,708
It's all very intriguing.

264
00:16:50,541 --> 00:16:54,333
Well, I did almost get wiped out earlier.

265
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:57,500
This place really does live up to
its savage reputation.

266
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,333
Hm? Its reputation?

267
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:03,166
You don't know? But you live here.

268
00:17:03,166 --> 00:17:04,041
Yeah...

269
00:17:04,041 --> 00:17:06,583
And you tamed all those beasts...

270
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:10,166
I'm not really sure
what you're talking about.

271
00:17:10,666 --> 00:17:13,416
Anyways, about that magic you're using...

272
00:17:13,416 --> 00:17:15,916
I've never seen any techniques
used to create stuff like that.

273
00:17:15,916 --> 00:17:17,875
Is that some kind of magic tool?

274
00:17:18,083 --> 00:17:20,500
A magic tool? Maybe.

275
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:23,291
Oh my, what a day it's been!

276
00:17:23,666 --> 00:17:28,125
I've lived a long life, but I guess there are
still a lot of things left for me to learn.

277
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:34,833
She's right.
It's been a day of surprises.

278
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:38,250
I can't believe I met her.

279
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:41,125
That's right.

280
00:17:41,125 --> 00:17:44,458
I don't know if something like this
will ever happen again.

281
00:17:44,458 --> 00:17:47,375
Hey, are you planning on
continuing to live here?

282
00:17:47,375 --> 00:17:50,583
If you are, would it be alright if
I came to visit again some time?

283
00:17:50,583 --> 00:17:51,666
I have a request!

284
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:53,541
If...

285
00:17:54,208 --> 00:17:56,041
If it's alright with you,

286
00:17:56,041 --> 00:17:58,416
would you stay here with me?

287
00:17:58,416 --> 00:17:59,250
Huh?

288
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:04,083
Well it'd be grateful if I could stay here
to work on my research a little longer...

289
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:06,125
I want you to live here with me!

290
00:18:06,125 --> 00:18:07,333
I want you here forever!

291
00:18:09,083 --> 00:18:11,083
Huh? D-do you mean...

292
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:12,083
Exactly!

293
00:18:13,583 --> 00:18:15,333
W-wait. Hold on!

294
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:17,708
This is all so sudden!

295
00:18:17,708 --> 00:18:19,708
I don't want to let this chance get away!

296
00:18:20,291 --> 00:18:25,250
But, I told you before...
there are people who are after me.

297
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:26,375
I don't care.

298
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:27,750
I'm a vampire!

299
00:18:27,750 --> 00:18:28,875
Not a problem!

300
00:18:35,375 --> 00:18:37,416
I'm surprised myself.

301
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:42,000
I've never been good at
dealing with other people.

302
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,833
The reason I came here was so that I could
live on my own, away from people.

303
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,041
But living here alone...

304
00:18:49,916 --> 00:18:52,750
I don't know how many more years
I can handle that.

305
00:18:58,416 --> 00:19:00,041
Okay, fine.

306
00:19:01,666 --> 00:19:03,583
I'm okay with it, but...

307
00:19:04,541 --> 00:19:07,041
it's just all so sudden.

308
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:07,916
So then...

309
00:19:07,916 --> 00:19:08,791
Then what?

310
00:19:08,791 --> 00:19:10,958
Um, I'm okay with staying to live here.

311
00:19:10,958 --> 00:19:12,625
It's not like I have anywhere else to go.

312
00:19:12,625 --> 00:19:13,458
Really?

313
00:19:13,458 --> 00:19:16,833
But we really have only just met each other.

314
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:20,208
We can get to know each other
while we're living together.

315
00:19:20,208 --> 00:19:22,625
It's just... so sudden.

316
00:19:24,291 --> 00:19:28,583
It was such a sudden proposal...

317
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:30,416
Proposal?

318
00:19:30,416 --> 00:19:33,041
You told me to stay and
live here with you, right?

319
00:19:33,041 --> 00:19:33,958
Oh yeah.

320
00:19:33,958 --> 00:19:36,833
It's pretty lonely here, so I thought it
would be nice if you were here with me.

321
00:19:36,833 --> 00:19:40,333
When you asked me to be with you forever,
that's what you meant, isn't it?!

322
00:19:41,875 --> 00:19:43,541
You're getting embarrassed now?!

323
00:19:43,541 --> 00:19:45,416
No, it's just...

324
00:19:45,416 --> 00:19:47,208
Okay. So I proposed to you.

325
00:19:47,625 --> 00:19:49,208
Is that not what you meant?

326
00:19:49,208 --> 00:19:50,208
It is what I meant!

327
00:19:50,208 --> 00:19:51,708
In fact, it's exactly what I want!

328
00:19:51,708 --> 00:19:52,875
I implore you!

329
00:19:53,458 --> 00:19:55,416
Stop! Alright already.

330
00:20:00,333 --> 00:20:04,625
Jeez... I told you okay, didn't I?

331
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,583
Yay!

332
00:20:12,458 --> 00:20:13,541
Thank you!

333
00:20:13,541 --> 00:20:17,875
I told you, you're moving too fast!

334
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:33,791
Good morning.

335
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,916
Good morning.

336
00:20:37,916 --> 00:20:41,250
I never thought a simple greeting
could make me so happy.

337
00:20:42,666 --> 00:20:44,250
Why did you get small again?

338
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:45,916
It's for my own protection.

339
00:20:45,916 --> 00:20:48,666
You won't think about touching me
as long as I look like this, right?

340
00:20:48,666 --> 00:20:51,208
Y-yeah... I'll restrain myself.

341
00:20:51,666 --> 00:20:53,833
So what are you working on now?

342
00:20:53,833 --> 00:20:57,166
Well, I was thinking of trying to grow
sweet potatoes next.

343
00:20:57,166 --> 00:20:58,250
Oh?

344
00:20:58,250 --> 00:21:00,208
They're easy to prepare and eat,
and they preserve well.

345
00:21:00,208 --> 00:21:01,666
And now we have more people living here.

346
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:05,666
That's right, you're the first person
to move in here.

347
00:21:05,666 --> 00:21:07,541
That makes you the first villager here.

348
00:21:07,541 --> 00:21:10,291
What do you mean?
This is a village?

349
00:21:10,291 --> 00:21:13,958
Well, not yet. It's still not at that level.

350
00:21:16,166 --> 00:21:18,666
You guys were living here first, weren't you?

351
00:21:18,666 --> 00:21:21,708
Then there's Zabuton and her family.
And she's got a bunch of kids.

352
00:21:21,708 --> 00:21:26,083
So Lu, that makes you...
about the 30th villager, I think.

353
00:21:26,541 --> 00:21:29,333
What kind of title is that?
Does it even matter at that point?

354
00:21:29,583 --> 00:21:33,791
I wanted to ask, do you think we can
grow medicinal herbs in this field?

355
00:21:34,375 --> 00:21:37,333
I think we might be able to.
Let's try it and find out.

356
00:21:37,333 --> 00:21:38,083
Yeah!

357
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:40,708
We'll have to find some way
to get our hands on the right seeds.

358
00:21:40,708 --> 00:21:43,625
Nope. We don't actually need any seeds.

359
00:21:43,625 --> 00:21:45,458
Huh? Why not?

360
00:23:23,541 --> 00:23:25,583
Yeah... I remember we talked about

361
00:23:25,583 --> 00:23:28,500
The Forest of Death on
the other side of the mountain.

362
00:23:28,916 --> 00:23:30,583
I see.

363
00:23:30,583 --> 00:23:34,458
Man, I've been seeing a lot of
strange customers in here lately.

364
00:23:34,458 --> 00:23:37,166
I don't know if you're searching for someone
or what, but you should give up.

365
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:39,958
Unless you can sprout wings and fly, that is.

366
00:23:40,416 --> 00:23:42,625
Very well. I understand.

367
00:23:42,625 --> 00:23:45,125
Thank you for your kindness.

368
00:23:47,041 --> 00:23:50,541
Next time
Episode 3
More and More New Roommates

